Z||000007||deceler8||04-19-2001||09:32 AM||||It's an '86...the steering wheel is courtesy of FieroDave and the car was originally equipped with wheel covers...just painted the steel wheels and put on center caps and the trim rings.<P>Interior was nice...seats not torn and everything was in good shape but the shift console...it was trashed. So I sanded all the paint off the shift plate (now gloss black) and made the oak shift console. It was an easy and cheap fix for the trashed piece.<P>Back about 1984, I test drove one exactly like this one and it's funny that I found one  like that almost 15 years later. Couldn't afford one when they were new...I sure could afford the $500 this one cost.||||reg||1
